    "title": "Graco recalls more than 5,000 SnugRide Turn & Slide baby seats",
    "text": "NEWSGraco recalls more than 5,000 baby seats. See model numbers Greg GiesenDelaware News JournalApril 14, 2026, 1:02 p.m. ETGraco is recalling 5,126 car seats because the infant seat carrier may detach from the base in a crash, according to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration.The recalled car seats are Graco SnugRide Turn & Slide models. The products were manufactured between Dec. 1, 2025, and March 27, 2026.The seats were sold between January and March 2026 at Amazon, Babylist, Target, Walmart and on GracoBaby.com.Ford recalling more than 425,000 vehicles. See which models Ford recalling more than 261,000 vehicles. See which models Hyundai recalling more than 61,000 vehicles. See which models Toyota recalling more than 550,000 thousand vehicles. See which models Ford recalling more than 2.3 million vehicles. See which models Ford recalling more than 4.8 million vehicles. See which models Mercedes-Benz recalls vehicles for fire risk. See which models Chrysler recalling more than 536,000 vehicles. See which models Hyundai recalling more than 610,000 vehicles. See which modelsThe SnugRide Turn & Slide Rotating Infant Car Seat model numbers included in the recall are:2231809 (black)2231806 (mulberry/girl plum)2231881 (black)2231887 (sandstone/tan)2231885 (sandstone/tan)2231884 (black)The SnugRide Turn & Slide Rotating Infant Car Seat base model number included in the recall is:2231810 (black)Owners are advised to install the child seat using the vehicle seat belt without the base until a replacement arrives. Graco will replace the child seat free of charge. For information on how to replace the car seat and available replacement options, visit Graco’s website.Owner notification letters are expected to be mailed this month. Owners may contact Graco customer service at 800‑345‑4109.MD Refused Assisted Living For His Dad (This Is What He Did Instead)The alternative that changed everything for his familyGekkoGifts | AdAdUndoAsk a Pro: \"I'm 65 W